+`S03`). For each defect the script changes one piece of text in one file, or two pieces where the
+defect needs both, and stops without running anything if the text it expects is not found exactly
+once. It runs the scenarios named for the defect (`--only=`), runs the whole gate if they report
+nothing, and puts the file back after every run, a crash included. A defect is *caught* when the
+gate reports at least one finding, any finding and not only the kind the defect was written for (the
+last column of the table says which came), and it *survives* when the whole gate reports none. A gate
+fault, or no report, in the run of the named scenarios is recorded as a fault and not as a catch; the
+whole-gate run is judged on its findings alone.
