+The arms did not work on the first full try. Bare `--broken` exited 2 with `NOT REFUTED` for
+`wrap`, `overflow`, `print` and `leak`, and the cause was three bugs in the plant script (a
+stylesheet added before the page had a root element, one record of planted nodes shared by three
+observers so that the first hid the other two (they now plant through one observer), and
+`default` setting a radio button's `checked` flag so that the app's own state never changed (it
+now presses the radio button). The first `live` arm replaced the area that React holds, which
+blanked the page and gave 3 faults; it now inserts a copy that a mutation observer keeps in step
+and hides the original.
